1. Definitions

"Software" means the source code, documentation, examples, configuration
files, and other materials distributed with this license.

"Covered Work" means:

  a. the Software or any substantial portion of it;
  b. any copy, modification, adaptation, translation, port, extension, or
     derivative work of the Software; and
  c. any implementation created by copying, translating, transforming, or
     materially adapting the Software's protectable source-code expression,
     structure, sequence, organization, or implementation details, even if
     names, formatting, programming language, or superficial structure have
     been changed.

An independently created implementation based only on unprotected ideas,
algorithms, interfaces, behavior, or functionality is not a Covered Work
unless applicable copyright law provides otherwise. An automated code
similarity score alone does not determine whether a work is covered; actual
copying, derivation, and substantial similarity of protected expression are
the relevant factors.

"Commercial Use" means any use primarily intended for or directed toward
commercial advantage, monetary compensation, or the operation of a
for-profit business. It includes, without limitation:

  a. selling, licensing, or charging for a Covered Work;
  b. offering a Covered Work or its output as a paid product, hosted service,
     software-as-a-service, consulting deliverable, or managed service;
  c. using a Covered Work internally for the operations, research,
     development, or competitive advantage of a for-profit entity;
  d. bundling a Covered Work with a commercial product or service;
  e. using a Covered Work to train, fine-tune, evaluate, or operate a model or
     system intended for commercial use; or
  f. removing, disguising, or rewriting the Software in order to avoid the
     restrictions of this license.

"Non-Commercial Purpose" means personal study, academic research, teaching,
evaluation, or use by a charitable or public-interest organization, provided
that the use is not performed for commercial advantage or compensation and
is not performed for or on behalf of a for-profit entity.

